; The makespan question, asked as a ladder of feasibility checks.
;
; Each property asks "can every job be finished by tick K". The SMALLEST K that
; holds is the optimal makespan, and its witness is the schedule that achieves
; it. Two are asked here rather than the whole range: the largest K that fails
; and the smallest that holds, which together pin the optimum from both sides.
(load "stdlib.pol")

(property done-by-4 "every job finished by tick 4 — the bound that is too tight"
  (possible (and (all (j job) (is j.stage done)) (is clk.at t4))))

(property done-by-5 "every job finished by tick 5 — the optimum"
  (possible (and (all (j job) (is j.stage done)) (is clk.at t5))))
